## Slide 2

KPI Calculations	

Allows the collection of real-time production counts and event information to record Interval records in the TrakSYS Database
An Interval contains raw data over a period of time (typically 30 to 60 minutes) that can be used to calculate Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Configurable at the System Level

OEE : An industry standard calculation for measuring Asset Effectiveness [ OEE = A * P * Q ]
Availability : % of time a process is available for Production
Performance : Ratio of Total Units vs. Theoretical over Available Time
Quality : Ratio of Good vs. Total Production
TEEP : A variation of OEE that re-interprets un-scheduled time as Availability Losses

Configuration

Common KPIs

## Slide 3

KPI Calculation Properties 

Interval Duration
A raw KPI data record is recorded every Interval Duration (minutes).
Update Interval 
Frequency that the Interval will be updated within an Interval Duration. 
Derived Input
One of the three Inputs that should be calculated based on the other two.

## Slide 4

KPI Calculation Properties 

Theoretical Rate
Maximum Calculation Units per minute the measured asset can be operated.
Target Rate
Ideal Calculation Units per minute the measured asset should be operated.
Calculation Units
Unit of measure for the smallest counted piece on produced on the System.

